xnu: 0090 sweet widen LEDGER_NAME_MAX 32 -> 40

Real-phone boot #18 dies inside init_task_ledgers with the panic
string swallowed; QEMU crosses the same window and reports
"couldn't create entries for task ledger template @task.c:1265".
Root cause: osfmk/kern/ledger.h clamps every ledger name to
LEDGER_NAME_MAX (32), but init_task_ledgers() registers an official
32-char key (purgeable_nonvolatile_compressed), so
ledger_entry_add_with_flags() hits strlen(key) >= LEDGER_NAME_MAX,
returns -1 and panics before any task ledger exists.  Upstream key
width, not a build-config problem.  Widen LEDGER_NAME_MAX to 40 so a
full 32-char official key plus NUL fits; every widened buffer
(ledger_info/ledger_template_info/ledger_entry_info, et_* names) is
kernel-internal only, so the size delta has no ABI exposure.
diff --git a/osfmk/kern/ledger.h b/osfmk/kern/ledger.h
--- a/osfmk/kern/ledger.h
+++ b/osfmk/kern/ledger.h
@@ -45,7 +45,10 @@
 /* LEDGER_MAX_CMD always tracks the index of the last ledger command. */
 #define LEDGER_MAX_CMD          LEDGER_LIMIT
 
-#define LEDGER_NAME_MAX 32
+/* Sweet 0090: widened 32->40; the official task-ledger keys
+ * purgeable_nonvolatile_compressed etc. need one full 32-char name plus NUL,
+ * and the widened name buffers are kernel-internal only (no ABI). */
+#define LEDGER_NAME_MAX 40
 
 struct ledger_info {
 	char    li_name[LEDGER_NAME_MAX];
